  "term": "Beck Anxiety Inventory",
  "definition": "The Beck Anxiety Inventory is an assessment measure used to evaluate anxiety symptoms. In the source material, it is listed as a neuropsychiatric outcome measure for comparing anxiety-related outcomes in people with Parkinson’s disease.",
